# Finish Checklist & Security Report

Before declaring relevant work complete, review **changed** code.

## Security (as applicable)

Secrets · auth · authz · rate limits · input validation · injection · XSS · CSRF · IDOR · mass assignment · path traversal · SSRF · command injection · uploads · sensitive logging · error leakage · CORS · headers · session/token safety · dependency vulns

## SEO / UX (public pages)

Title · meta description · canonical · index/noindex · H1/hierarchy · URL slug · internal links · alt text · images · responsive · CWV · OG/`og:image` · structured data · HTTPS · sitemap · robots.txt · production URLs

## Implementation order

1. Understand architecture → 2. Security/SEO implications → 3. Smallest maintainable change → 4. Server-side validation → 5. Server-side authz → 6. Rate-limit abuse paths → 7. No secrets in code/client → 8. Preserve behavior → 9. A11y/mobile/SEO/perf → 10. Checklist → 11. Report remaining risks

## Substantial security changes — brief report

1. **Risk addressed** — attack surface
2. **Changes made** — controls added
3. **Remaining risks** — assumptions/limits
4. **Secrets discovered** — if yes, say rotate/revoke (not only move to env)
5. **Infrastructure** — HTTPS, WAF, Redis, secret manager, Search Console, CDN, DB perms, etc.

**Non-negotiable:** Secure, SEO-friendly, accessible, and responsive by default — without unnecessary architecture churn.
